CORE libcxx
visit.cpp
--cpp20 --stdlib libc++ --object-bits 12
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ visit: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
dropped the body of system-header function
--
libc++ (LLVM 18) std::visit(F, variant<int, char>).  The layers that dropped
its body: the declaration's default template argument
(cpp11_default_template_argument_from_earlier_declaration), a friend of a
base class (cpp11_friend_of_base_accesses_member_through_derived), nested
pack expansions (cpp11_function_parameter_pack_in_nested_expansion),
explicit pack arguments (cpp11_explicit_pack_arguments_before_deduced_pack),
a class template pack in a function parameter pack expansion
(cpp11_class_pack_and_function_parameter_pack_in_one_expansion), the size
of a function parameter pack (cpp17_function_parameter_pack_after_non_type_
pack), folds over a later pack (cpp17_fold_over_later_pack_in_constexpr_
member), an empty function parameter pack
(cpp17_empty_function_parameter_pack_with_several_template_packs) and the
properties' function name (cpp11_statement_after_local_class_member_
function).  clang++ 18 -stdlib=libc++ accepts this program, and it fails
only its WRONG assertion.
